CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++ --show-goto-functions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
statement="member_initializer"
statement="default"
statement="cpp-using"
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/11: tuple's constructor template instantiated for no
arguments is never odr-used, so its mem-initializer is never converted.
Its body used to reach goto conversion in parse form and became an OTHER
instruction `statement="member_initializer"' (on bin53), on which
symbolic execution aborts (symex_other.cpp "Unreachable") if a path ever
reaches it.  The front end now drops a body that still holds such a
statement; a never-converted body is dropped silently, since the member
is not instantiated at all.  clang++ 18 with libc++ accepts the program.
